1
00:00:05,140 --> 00:00:06,760
How's your mom holding up?

2
00:00:06,760 --> 00:00:09,780
She's doing okay, but we just lost another nurse.

3
00:00:09,780 --> 00:00:11,450
- How many is that now? - Two,

4
00:00:11,450 --> 00:00:12,830
and I know what you're thinking--

5
00:00:12,830 --> 00:00:14,490
she's eating them.

6
00:00:16,870 --> 00:00:19,270
She's just so impossible, they keep quitting.

7
00:00:19,270 --> 00:00:20,780
So, who's watching her now?

8
00:00:20,780 --> 00:00:24,040
A bowl full of M & M's with a few Ambien tossed in.

9
00:00:24,970 --> 00:00:25,940
What up, guys?

10
00:00:25,940 --> 00:00:27,340
- Hello. - Hey. Hello.

11
00:00:28,170 --> 00:00:29,040
Okay.

12
00:00:29,560 --> 00:00:31,210
Well, now that everyone's here,

13
00:00:31,210 --> 00:00:33,500
Penny and I have some big news.

14
00:00:33,530 --> 00:00:35,070
We're engaged!

15
00:00:35,070 --> 00:00:36,070
Oh my God!

16
00:00:41,210 --> 00:00:43,870
And I thought me having sex with Emily was gonna be the big news.

17
00:00:50,560 --> 00:00:52,240
What the hell!

18
00:00:53,090 --> 00:00:54,620
You guys propose all the time.

19
00:00:54,620 --> 00:00:56,420
This never happens.

20
00:00:57,310 --> 00:00:58,150
You're right!

21
00:01:26,460 --> 00:01:28,900
Boy, I'm so hungry today.

22
00:01:29,420 --> 00:01:31,420
I wonder why?

23
00:01:33,010 --> 00:01:35,510
Because you had sex the other night?

24
00:01:35,610 --> 00:01:37,300
You know what?

25
00:01:37,300 --> 00:01:39,330
That may be it.

26
00:01:40,710 --> 00:01:43,130
By the way, it isn't like riding a bike.

27
00:01:43,130 --> 00:01:45,500
Like, I fell off a few times.

28
00:01:48,040 --> 00:01:49,180
Hey, buddy.

29
00:01:49,180 --> 00:01:50,560
Hello.

30
00:01:50,560 --> 00:01:52,170
You okay?

31
00:01:53,200 --> 00:01:56,330
I just got called into President Siebert's office.

32
00:01:56,330 --> 00:01:57,940
The university won't let me

33
00:01:57,940 --> 00:02:01,430
switch my field of study to inflationary cosmology.

34
00:02:01,430 --> 00:02:04,420
They're forcing me to continue with string theory.

35
00:02:04,420 --> 00:02:05,470
Why?

36
00:02:05,470 --> 00:02:07,330
He said it's why they hired me,

37
00:02:07,330 --> 00:02:09,690
it's-it's what my grant was designated for,

38
00:02:09,690 --> 00:02:13,100
and that everybody has to do things they don't want to do.

39
00:02:13,100 --> 00:02:15,040
He then gave an example of something he had to do,

40
00:02:15,040 --> 00:02:16,050
even though he didn't want to,

41
00:02:16,050 --> 00:02:18,610
which was look at my stupid face.

42
00:02:20,400 --> 00:02:22,370
That's a rude thing to say.

43
00:02:22,370 --> 00:02:24,310
Out loud.

44
00:02:25,980 --> 00:02:27,230
It's an outrage.

45
00:02:27,230 --> 00:02:30,490
Honestly, I'm tempted to leave the university.

46
00:02:30,490 --> 00:02:32,110
You know, if you're really serious about that,

47
00:02:32,110 --> 00:02:34,690
I hear there are some exciting opportunities

48
00:02:34,690 --> 00:02:37,440
in home care for the old and fat.

49
00:02:38,520 --> 00:02:41,420
Whatever you do, just don't make any rash decisions.

50
00:02:41,420 --> 00:02:42,480
I don't know.

51
00:02:42,480 --> 00:02:44,640
I am really aggravated.

52
00:02:45,240 --> 00:02:47,990
When I'm feeling low, I have sex with a girl.

53
00:02:49,700 --> 00:02:51,470
But that's just me.

54
00:02:55,190 --> 00:02:57,330
- Oh, come on, give her a chance. - No.

55
00:02:57,360 --> 00:02:59,490
Life, it is too short.

56
00:03:00,980 --> 00:03:02,900
I know you've only been here a day and a half,

57
00:03:02,900 --> 00:03:05,170
but you're like part of the family!

58
00:03:07,210 --> 00:03:10,230
I don't think the service is gonna send any more people.

59
00:03:10,230 --> 00:03:15,920
Yeah, maybe it's time we just release Ma back into the sea.

60
00:03:17,730 --> 00:03:18,830
That's not helpful.

61
00:03:18,830 --> 00:03:21,970
Well, then, we may need to get used to the idea

62
00:03:21,970 --> 00:03:25,640
that we're gonna be living here the next few months.

63
00:03:25,640 --> 00:03:26,610
But we have jobs.

64
00:03:26,610 --> 00:03:29,090
We can't baby-sit her 24 hours a day.

65
00:03:29,090 --> 00:03:32,000
Well, what if we use our vacation time?

66
00:03:32,000 --> 00:03:35,560
I wanted to go to Hawaii, not Hell.

67
00:03:36,240 --> 00:03:38,000
I don't know what else we can do.

68
00:03:38,470 --> 00:03:41,140
Howie, I love you,

69
00:03:41,200 --> 00:03:43,340
and as your wife, your mother is every bit

70
00:03:43,340 --> 00:03:46,620
as much my problem as she is yours, so...

71
00:03:47,240 --> 00:03:49,690
I want a divorce.

72
00:03:53,370 --> 00:03:54,850
Hello, Leonard.

73
00:03:54,850 --> 00:03:56,160
Hi, Mom.

74
00:03:56,160 --> 00:03:58,500
I have some exciting news.

75
00:03:58,500 --> 00:04:00,550
I'm listening.

76
00:04:01,490 --> 00:04:02,710
Before I tell you,

77
00:04:02,710 --> 00:04:05,050
will you promise to try and be happy for me

78
00:04:05,050 --> 00:04:08,150
and keep any concerns you have to yourself?

79
00:04:08,590 --> 00:04:09,840
No.

80
00:04:11,590 --> 00:04:15,460
Let me save you all of your hemming and hawing.

81
00:04:15,460 --> 00:04:19,010
Sheldon already told me that you and Penny are engaged.

82
00:04:19,780 --> 00:04:23,000
I-I hate that you talk to him more than you talk to me.

83
00:04:23,000 --> 00:04:25,990
Would you like for you and me to talk more?

84
00:04:27,680 --> 00:04:29,690
You know what? It's probably fine.

85
00:04:30,430 --> 00:04:34,400
In any event, while I've had my misgivings about...

86
00:04:35,050 --> 00:04:36,370
Penny...

87
00:04:37,560 --> 00:04:39,630
...Sheldon spoke very fondly of her,

88
00:04:39,630 --> 00:04:41,620
and if she is good enough for him,

89
00:04:41,620 --> 00:04:44,420
then she's good enough for me.

90
00:04:46,410 --> 00:04:47,770
I'm your son.

91
00:04:47,770 --> 00:04:51,070
What about the fact that she's good enough for me?

92
00:04:51,990 --> 00:04:53,500
Sure.

93
00:04:55,260 --> 00:04:56,330
Thanks, Mom.

94
00:04:56,330 --> 00:04:59,160
Leonard, would it make you feel better to hear that

95
00:04:59,160 --> 00:05:03,160
your mother approved of your life choices?

96
00:05:04,200 --> 00:05:05,710
Yes, it would.

97
00:05:05,710 --> 00:05:09,300
Yeah. Well, you should work on that.

98
00:05:13,190 --> 00:05:14,550
No, Mom, it's the same guy

99
00:05:14,550 --> 00:05:17,120
I've been going out with for the past two years.

100
00:05:17,120 --> 00:05:18,880
Yeah, the scientist.

101
00:05:19,600 --> 00:05:21,040
Well, it's complicated.

102
00:05:21,040 --> 00:05:24,750
I mean, he works with lasers and atomic magnets.

103
00:05:28,000 --> 00:05:29,840
No, I did not see it coming.

104
00:05:29,840 --> 00:05:31,770
No, we did not set a date.

105
00:05:32,120 --> 00:05:34,120
No, I am not pregnant.

106
00:05:35,050 --> 00:05:37,420
Yeah, this is a first for our family.

107
00:05:37,950 --> 00:05:39,680
All right, tell Dad I love him. I gotta go.

108
00:05:39,680 --> 00:05:40,940
All right, bye.

109
00:05:40,940 --> 00:05:42,790
- Atomic magnets? - Shut up.

110
00:05:45,380 --> 00:05:46,320
Sorry I'm late.

111
00:05:46,320 --> 00:05:47,260
The leaf blower broke,

112
00:05:47,260 --> 00:05:49,580
so I had to hand-dry my mother-in-law.

113
00:05:51,190 --> 00:05:52,110
You want some wine?

114
00:05:52,110 --> 00:05:53,380
Thanks.

115
00:05:53,440 --> 00:05:56,260
Little warning before you jump into this marriage business:

116
00:05:56,260 --> 00:05:57,440
You're not just marrying him,

117
00:05:57,440 --> 00:05:58,800
you're marrying his family.

118
00:05:58,800 --> 00:06:00,790
I think Leonard's mom's okay with me.

119
00:06:00,790 --> 00:06:02,090
It doesn't matter if she's okay with you.

120
00:06:02,090 --> 00:06:05,320
The question is: Can she go to the bathroom by herself?

121
00:06:11,080 --> 00:06:12,850
Hit me again.

122
00:06:14,350 --> 00:06:16,700
So, what are the living arrangements gonna be?

123
00:06:16,700 --> 00:06:18,420
Well, haven't really talked about it yet,

124
00:06:18,420 --> 00:06:19,670
but I figure, at some point,

125
00:06:19,670 --> 00:06:21,850
I'll move in with him, or he'll move in with me.

126
00:06:21,850 --> 00:06:24,470
Well, with you not working, that makes financial sense.

127
00:06:24,470 --> 00:06:25,620
You're not working!

128
00:06:25,620 --> 00:06:28,250
How would you like a job in home health care?

129
00:06:28,960 --> 00:06:30,410
Not a chance.

130
00:06:30,410 --> 00:06:32,040
- Please. I'm desperate. - No.

131
00:06:32,040 --> 00:06:34,690
- I'll pay you anything you want. - Okay, then, yeah.

132
00:06:36,050 --> 00:06:38,730
No! Keep your money!

133
00:06:42,530 --> 00:06:45,790
I could've ridden a bull longer than that.

134
00:06:48,420 --> 00:06:50,000
What you working on?

135
00:06:50,560 --> 00:06:53,230
I'm writing an appeal to the Faculty Senate,

136
00:06:53,230 --> 00:06:55,520
so that I can move on from string theory.

137
00:06:55,520 --> 00:06:56,990
Oh. How's it going?

138
00:06:57,840 --> 00:06:59,320
You tell me.

139
00:07:00,290 --> 00:07:02,280
"Dear Esteemed Colleagues,

140
00:07:02,280 --> 00:07:05,570
as you may know, I have requested to change my field of study.

141
00:07:05,570 --> 00:07:07,620
My decision to do so is, I believe,

142
00:07:07,620 --> 00:07:09,600
in the best interest of science.

143
00:07:09,600 --> 00:07:12,180
At your convenience, I'd be happy to explain it to you

144
00:07:12,180 --> 00:07:14,380
in words you'll understand."

145
00:07:16,750 --> 00:07:19,510
It's nice that you called them "Esteemed."

146
00:07:20,090 --> 00:07:21,980
You're right. I'll take that out.

147
00:07:23,830 --> 00:07:27,280
So, listen, there was something I was hoping to float past you.

148
00:07:27,280 --> 00:07:29,210
Now that Penny and I are engaged,

149
00:07:29,210 --> 00:07:31,880
I thought we might want to talk about our living arrangements.

150
00:07:32,450 --> 00:07:33,790
Of course.

151
00:07:33,790 --> 00:07:35,590
She's spent many nights here,

152
00:07:35,590 --> 00:07:38,160
and you're worried about preserving

153
00:07:38,160 --> 00:07:41,070
the myth of her virginity before the wedding.

154
00:07:44,270 --> 00:07:44,970
I'm not.

155
00:07:44,970 --> 00:07:46,800
Good, because not only has that ship sailed,

156
00:07:46,800 --> 00:07:50,310
if it hit an iceberg, countless men would perish.

157
00:07:51,940 --> 00:07:54,830
Actually, this is about where she and I are going to live.

158
00:07:54,830 --> 00:07:56,320
What do you mean?

159
00:07:57,270 --> 00:07:59,020
Well... well, we might want to live together.

160
00:07:59,020 --> 00:08:02,460
Oh, yeah, well, I've already given this some thought,

161
00:08:02,460 --> 00:08:03,250
and...

162
00:08:03,250 --> 00:08:06,510
I'm willing to let Penny live with us

163
00:08:06,820 --> 00:08:10,240
one day a week for a trial period.

164
00:08:11,510 --> 00:08:14,280
Now, obviously, not when she's made cranky

165
00:08:14,280 --> 00:08:16,850
by the shedding of her uterine lining.

166
00:08:19,390 --> 00:08:20,870
That's very sweet.

167
00:08:22,180 --> 00:08:26,510
But we were thinking more of us maybe living together with...

168
00:08:27,110 --> 00:08:28,960
not you.

169
00:08:31,380 --> 00:08:33,440
I don't understand.

170
00:08:34,700 --> 00:08:38,270
How could we all live together if I'm not there?

171
00:08:39,560 --> 00:08:41,950
Look, I-I know this is... this is change,

172
00:08:41,950 --> 00:08:43,220
and that sounds scary, but...

173
00:08:43,220 --> 00:08:44,880
Where are you going to go?

174
00:08:44,880 --> 00:08:46,410
I don't know.

175
00:08:46,410 --> 00:08:48,260
We just started to think about this.

176
00:08:48,260 --> 00:08:50,050
Maybe I'll move in with Penny,

177
00:08:50,050 --> 00:08:51,700
or maybe she and I'll take this place,

178
00:08:51,700 --> 00:08:53,080
and you can move across the hall.

179
00:08:53,080 --> 00:08:55,460
Move across the hall?!

180
00:08:56,030 --> 00:08:58,590
Did you take a marijuana?!

181
00:09:01,500 --> 00:09:03,150
No, I did not.

182
00:09:03,150 --> 00:09:05,800
Did you get hit on the head with a coconut?

183
00:09:06,740 --> 00:09:08,960
- No. - Well, then, I'm all out of guesses.

184
00:09:08,960 --> 00:09:10,380
What? Me move across the hall--

185
00:09:10,380 --> 00:09:12,250
Why would you even suggest such a thing?

186
00:09:12,250 --> 00:09:13,890
Because I love Penny,

187
00:09:13,890 --> 00:09:16,600
and want to give her the life she deserves.

188
00:09:16,820 --> 00:09:18,140
I see.

189
00:09:18,140 --> 00:09:21,910
You're putting your future bride's happiness above mine.

190
00:09:24,070 --> 00:09:25,960
Well, yeah.

191
00:09:35,090 --> 00:09:38,780
How dare the university force me to go back to string theory!

192
00:09:38,780 --> 00:09:40,460
They just don't appreciate you.

193
00:09:40,460 --> 00:09:41,950
Yeah, and on top of that,

194
00:09:41,950 --> 00:09:43,780
Leonard has the audacity to suggest that

195
00:09:43,780 --> 00:09:45,240
now that he and Penny are engaged,

196
00:09:45,240 --> 00:09:47,290
he may not want to live with me anymore.

197
00:09:47,290 --> 00:09:49,470
Here, I made you some Strawberry Quik.

198
00:09:49,470 --> 00:09:51,680
I have real problems here, Amy.

199
00:09:51,680 --> 00:09:54,870
I can't be mollified with a beverage designed for children.

200
00:09:55,220 --> 00:09:57,430
Mmm! Yummy.

201
00:09:58,840 --> 00:10:00,610
You know, this might work out for the best.

202
00:10:00,610 --> 00:10:02,240
I mean, you're always complaining about

203
00:10:02,240 --> 00:10:04,380
what a terrible roommate Leonard is.

204
00:10:04,380 --> 00:10:06,920
Like how he turns up the thermostat when you're not there.

205
00:10:07,570 --> 00:10:09,940
It's like walking into the Amazon.

206
00:10:10,430 --> 00:10:12,490
And not the good Amazon with one-day shipping.

207
00:10:12,510 --> 00:10:15,940
The awful one with birds and snakes.

208
00:10:16,150 --> 00:10:18,870
You hate the sound of all those keys on his key chain.

209
00:10:18,870 --> 00:10:20,810
Four keys!

210
00:10:20,810 --> 00:10:23,300
Who does he think he is, a warden?

211
00:10:24,870 --> 00:10:26,960
See? Maybe you'll love living alone.

212
00:10:26,960 --> 00:10:30,080
I don't know. Perhaps.

213
00:10:30,080 --> 00:10:32,330
And if it turns out you don't...

214
00:10:32,680 --> 00:10:34,100
you and I could live together.

215
00:10:34,100 --> 00:10:36,710
You and... Oh, sure.

216
00:10:37,110 --> 00:10:39,270
And while we're at it, why don't we get engaged, too?

217
00:10:39,320 --> 00:10:41,380
Why don't we get a little house, start a family?

218
00:10:41,380 --> 00:10:43,170
Enjoy our sunset years together?

219
00:10:43,170 --> 00:10:45,470
Do you hear yourself, woman?!

220
00:10:46,970 --> 00:10:48,380
Sheldon, it was just a thought.

221
00:10:48,380 --> 00:10:49,650
No. Here's a thought.

222
00:10:49,650 --> 00:10:50,880
You're not moving in,

223
00:10:50,880 --> 00:10:51,910
Leonard's not moving out,

224
00:10:51,910 --> 00:10:54,070
everything stays exactly the way it is.

225
00:10:54,070 --> 00:10:55,470
Yeah, and by the way,

226
00:10:55,470 --> 00:10:57,670
I saw you make this Strawberry Quik with syrup,

227
00:10:57,670 --> 00:10:59,690
and you're supposed to use the powder!

228
00:11:00,930 --> 00:11:01,880
It tastes the same.

229
00:11:01,880 --> 00:11:04,930
No. The syrup tastes better and I don't like it.

230
00:11:08,220 --> 00:11:09,700
This is so sweet!

231
00:11:09,700 --> 00:11:11,600
- You never cook for me. - Well...

232
00:11:11,600 --> 00:11:13,870
you cook for me all the time and...

233
00:11:17,290 --> 00:11:18,420
If you don't like my cooking,

234
00:11:18,420 --> 00:11:19,800
why haven't you ever said anything?

235
00:11:20,050 --> 00:11:23,580
It's hard to talk with so much heavy chewing to do.

236
00:11:24,740 --> 00:11:26,430
Sorry. I'll get better.

237
00:11:26,450 --> 00:11:29,110
I know you'll try.

238
00:11:29,830 --> 00:11:32,900
So, should we talk about setting a date?

239
00:11:32,900 --> 00:11:35,460
Well, I'd like to pick one that works with my brother's schedule.

240
00:11:35,460 --> 00:11:37,400
Okay. And when would that be?

241
00:11:37,400 --> 00:11:40,910
Uh, 12 to 18 months from now, depending on good behavior.

242
00:11:43,170 --> 00:11:44,400
Hi, is Sheldon here?

243
00:11:44,400 --> 00:11:46,010
No, I thought he was with you.

244
00:11:46,360 --> 00:11:47,680
He was, but he stormed off

245
00:11:47,680 --> 00:11:49,240
and now he isn't answering his phone.

246
00:11:49,240 --> 00:11:50,150
What happened?

247
00:11:50,150 --> 00:11:52,610
He was really angry that you suggested he move out.

248
00:11:53,500 --> 00:11:55,410
I also mentioned that he and I could live together

249
00:11:55,410 --> 00:11:56,580
but he was too mad at you to realize

250
00:11:56,580 --> 00:11:58,750
what a great idea that is.

251
00:12:00,970 --> 00:12:03,070
Well, he's been having a couple of tough days.

252
00:12:03,070 --> 00:12:04,370
I'm sure he's fine. He probably just

253
00:12:04,370 --> 00:12:06,950
needs a little alone time to decompress.

254
00:12:06,950 --> 00:12:08,200
You're probably right.

255
00:12:09,070 --> 00:12:10,590
So, what are you guys doing?

256
00:12:13,220 --> 00:12:16,250
Well, Leonard cooked for me and now we're just having

257
00:12:16,250 --> 00:12:19,690
a nice dinner, you know, as a newly engaged couple.

258
00:12:19,690 --> 00:12:21,720
That's nice.

259
00:12:26,940 --> 00:12:28,720
Anyway, as I was saying,

260
00:12:28,720 --> 00:12:32,400
Sheldon probably just needs a little alone time.

261
00:12:33,550 --> 00:12:36,010
'Cause that's important.

262
00:12:38,090 --> 00:12:40,280
Not just for him, but for...

263
00:12:41,230 --> 00:12:43,180
most anybody, really.

264
00:12:43,610 --> 00:12:45,860
Don't I know it.

265
00:12:45,860 --> 00:12:46,980
What is that, polenta?

266
00:12:46,980 --> 00:12:48,800
- Amy, get out. - Right.

267
00:12:54,310 --> 00:12:56,400
No.

268
00:12:59,220 --> 00:13:00,670
Hey, Sheldon.

269
00:13:00,670 --> 00:13:02,030
What happened?

270
00:13:02,030 --> 00:13:04,060
I was cooking in the back room last night

271
00:13:04,060 --> 00:13:06,200
and the hot plate caught on fire.

272
00:13:06,950 --> 00:13:08,290
And you couldn't put it out?

273
00:13:08,290 --> 00:13:09,590
I was across the street

274
00:13:09,590 --> 00:13:12,440
at the do-it-yourself car wash, taking a shower.

275
00:13:15,620 --> 00:13:17,560
So when will you reopen?

276
00:13:17,560 --> 00:13:18,960
Um, I don't know.

277
00:13:18,960 --> 00:13:21,630
I'm waiting to hear back from the insurance company.

278
00:13:22,730 --> 00:13:24,850
So, tomorrow?

279
00:13:25,870 --> 00:13:28,090
I don't mean to be rude, Sheldon, but, uh,

280
00:13:28,090 --> 00:13:30,110
my life is kind of falling apart right now.

281
00:13:30,110 --> 00:13:31,450
Your life?

282
00:13:31,450 --> 00:13:34,200
The university is making me do string theory

283
00:13:34,200 --> 00:13:38,320
and my girlfriend loves me so much she wants to live with me.

284
00:13:39,070 --> 00:13:41,310
And now, the place I need to go when I'm sad

285
00:13:41,310 --> 00:13:44,510
is damp and smells funny.

286
00:13:45,590 --> 00:13:47,730
Well, sorry I let you down.

287
00:13:47,730 --> 00:13:48,660
No.

288
00:13:48,660 --> 00:13:50,460
I do not accept this.

289
00:13:50,460 --> 00:13:52,510
Everything is changing and I hate it.

290
00:13:52,510 --> 00:13:53,760
It stops now.

291
00:13:53,760 --> 00:13:56,010
I'm helping you get back on your feet.

292
00:13:57,580 --> 00:14:00,370
I would like to purchase this comic book, please.

293
00:14:02,270 --> 00:14:03,990
That'll be $2.99.

294
00:14:03,990 --> 00:14:06,350
Really? It's soaking wet.

295
00:14:07,300 --> 00:14:09,210
Fine, a dollar.

296
00:14:11,750 --> 00:14:12,860
Can you break a 20?

297
00:14:12,860 --> 00:14:15,130
No, I only have hundreds.

298
00:14:16,410 --> 00:14:17,740
You know what?

299
00:14:18,230 --> 00:14:21,020
I don't always recognize sarcasm, but I do right now,

300
00:14:21,020 --> 00:14:22,670
and I don't appreciate it.

301
00:14:22,670 --> 00:14:24,480
I'm sorry for your loss.

302
00:14:24,480 --> 00:14:27,790
But you're not the only one whose day has been a disaster.

303
00:14:34,970 --> 00:14:37,400
That could have killed me.

304
00:14:37,880 --> 00:14:40,540
I can't catch a break.

305
00:14:43,090 --> 00:14:44,900
I haven't heard from Sheldon in a while.

306
00:14:44,900 --> 00:14:46,000
You think he's okay?

307
00:14:46,000 --> 00:14:47,970
Oh, I'm sure he's fine.

308
00:14:47,970 --> 00:14:49,840
I'm gonna see where he is.

309
00:14:50,270 --> 00:14:51,080
How?

310
00:14:51,080 --> 00:14:53,870
Oh, I know his password, so I can track his phone.

311
00:14:54,130 --> 00:14:55,310
You do that?

312
00:14:55,310 --> 00:14:56,500
Not always,

313
00:14:56,500 --> 00:14:59,030
but ever since he wandered off at the swap meet chasing a balloon,

314
00:14:59,030 --> 00:15:00,920
I get worried.

315
00:15:01,840 --> 00:15:03,050
He can take care of himself.

316
00:15:03,050 --> 00:15:04,820
Look, we went over stranger danger

317
00:15:04,820 --> 00:15:06,620
and gave him that whistle.

318
00:15:07,970 --> 00:15:09,900
- That's weird. - What?

319
00:15:09,900 --> 00:15:11,720
He's at the train station.

320
00:15:11,720 --> 00:15:13,550
So? He loves trains.

321
00:15:13,550 --> 00:15:15,660
It's dark out and he's alone, I don't like it.

322
00:15:15,660 --> 00:15:16,840
Let's go get him.

323
00:15:17,540 --> 00:15:19,130
Oh, it's sweet how you look out for him.

324
00:15:19,130 --> 00:15:20,190
You're a good guy.

325
00:15:20,190 --> 00:15:21,450
It's not just that.

326
00:15:21,450 --> 00:15:24,340
My mother would kill me if I let something happen to him.

327
00:15:28,310 --> 00:15:31,120
Dude, I'm so sorry.

328
00:15:31,120 --> 00:15:32,410
Don't take this the wrong way,

329
00:15:32,410 --> 00:15:35,200
but did you do this for the insurance money?

330
00:15:35,200 --> 00:15:38,400
No. God, you sound like the police, the firemen,

331
00:15:38,400 --> 00:15:41,670
my parents, my therapist and the insurance company.

332
00:15:42,760 --> 00:15:44,800
We're here for you, man. Whatever you need, okay?

333
00:15:44,800 --> 00:15:46,410
Uh, actually, I was wondering if I could

334
00:15:46,410 --> 00:15:48,290
crash at your place for a few nights.

335
00:15:48,290 --> 00:15:49,600
Sure, of course.

336
00:15:49,600 --> 00:15:51,990
Oh, actually, Emily was gonna spend the night.

337
00:15:51,990 --> 00:15:54,300
You slept with her? Nice.

338
00:15:54,300 --> 00:15:56,310
Well, I can't take all the credit.

339
00:15:56,310 --> 00:15:58,510
She let me do it to her, but...

340
00:16:00,610 --> 00:16:03,090
Uh, but I can always call her and cancel.

341
00:16:03,090 --> 00:16:05,370
Hang on. I know a place you can stay

342
00:16:05,370 --> 00:16:07,710
and earn some money at the same time.

343
00:16:07,710 --> 00:16:09,380
- Great. - I just have to warn you,

344
00:16:09,380 --> 00:16:14,460
it'll involve humiliation, degradation and verbal abuse.

345
00:16:14,460 --> 00:16:17,370
So what's the catch?

346
00:16:22,870 --> 00:16:24,230
Sheldon.

347
00:16:25,070 --> 00:16:27,040
You tracked my phone?

348
00:16:27,040 --> 00:16:27,990
Yeah.

349
00:16:27,990 --> 00:16:32,640
Boy, you chase one balloon for three miles.

350
00:16:34,370 --> 00:16:36,330
We were worried about you.

351
00:16:36,330 --> 00:16:38,260
Don't be melodramatic.

352
00:16:38,260 --> 00:16:41,250
I'm just getting on a train and leaving forever.

353
00:16:42,630 --> 00:16:43,350
Seriously?

354
00:16:43,350 --> 00:16:46,340
You don't even have a change of clothes or a toothbrush.

355
00:16:46,340 --> 00:16:49,270
My plan is to stop at malls and buy what I need.

356
00:16:49,270 --> 00:16:51,620
It's called living off the land.

357
00:16:52,740 --> 00:16:53,790
Okay, I know you're upset

358
00:16:53,790 --> 00:16:55,520
and there's a lot of stuff going on,

359
00:16:55,520 --> 00:16:57,260
but it's nothing we can't work out.

360
00:16:57,260 --> 00:16:58,500
Come on, let's get you home.

361
00:16:58,500 --> 00:17:00,920
No. I've reached my breaking point.

362
00:17:00,920 --> 00:17:02,850
I need to leave. Now.

363
00:17:02,850 --> 00:17:04,050
And go where?

364
00:17:04,050 --> 00:17:05,630
It doesn't matter.

365
00:17:05,630 --> 00:17:08,770
So a few things don't go your way

366
00:17:08,770 --> 00:17:12,750
and your best decision is to ride the rails like a hobo?

367
00:17:14,700 --> 00:17:16,500
I suppose it is.

368
00:17:16,500 --> 00:17:18,500
Except I have a credit card.

369
00:17:18,500 --> 00:17:21,660
And I refuse to carry my laptop at the end of a stick.

370
00:17:24,670 --> 00:17:27,780
And I'd sooner die than eat beans out of a can.

371
00:17:29,100 --> 00:17:30,180
Come on, come home with us

372
00:17:30,180 --> 00:17:32,330
and tomorrow I'll-I'll take you to Legoland.

373
00:17:32,330 --> 00:17:35,220
Legoland is not the solution to everything.

374
00:17:35,960 --> 00:17:37,020
And it's too much of a scene

375
00:17:37,020 --> 00:17:39,200
since that movie came out.

376
00:17:40,990 --> 00:17:42,740
Then what can I do?

377
00:17:42,740 --> 00:17:45,170
Leonard, I am overwhelmed.

378
00:17:45,170 --> 00:17:48,450
Everything is changing and it's simply too much.

379
00:17:48,450 --> 00:17:50,520
I need to get away and think.

380
00:17:50,520 --> 00:17:53,050
Oh, c-come on, you know you're overreacting.

381
00:17:53,050 --> 00:17:53,930
Leonard, hang on.

382
00:17:53,930 --> 00:17:55,930
Just... come here for a second.

383
00:17:58,370 --> 00:18:00,100
Maybe we need to let him go.

384
00:18:00,100 --> 00:18:01,730
What?! Why?

385
00:18:01,730 --> 00:18:02,930
It might be good for him.

386
00:18:02,930 --> 00:18:05,960
Y-You know he can't take a trip like this by himself.

387
00:18:05,960 --> 00:18:07,220
He's a grown man.

388
00:18:07,220 --> 00:18:10,210
No, he looks like a grown man.

389
00:18:11,630 --> 00:18:12,840
You've seen Freaky Friday,

390
00:18:12,840 --> 00:18:15,930
sometimes little kids end up in big person bodies.

391
00:18:17,360 --> 00:18:19,630
Leonard, we can't protect him forever.

392
00:18:19,630 --> 00:18:20,810
I know, but...

393
00:18:20,810 --> 00:18:22,540
He'll be okay.

394
00:18:22,540 --> 00:18:24,550
You taught him well, Padawan.

395
00:18:24,550 --> 00:18:25,520
Good Lord!

396
00:18:25,520 --> 00:18:28,580
Padawan's the student, not the teacher.

397
00:18:30,790 --> 00:18:32,590
Seriously, let him go.

398
00:18:38,700 --> 00:18:40,240
Sheldon, if you really need to do this,

399
00:18:40,240 --> 00:18:42,130
I'm not gonna stand in your way.

400
00:18:42,960 --> 00:18:44,420
I do.

401
00:18:45,300 --> 00:18:46,730
Okay.

402
00:18:47,630 --> 00:18:48,820
Good luck.

403
00:18:52,720 --> 00:18:54,910
Be safe and call us.

404
00:18:57,810 --> 00:18:59,370
I will.

405
00:19:01,630 --> 00:19:02,900
Bye, buddy.

406
00:19:07,660 --> 00:19:09,140
Sheldon...

407
00:19:09,140 --> 00:19:10,870
Yes?

408
00:19:11,440 --> 00:19:13,550
I'm gonna miss you.

409
00:19:14,160 --> 00:19:16,350
Of course you are.

410
00:19:18,560 --> 00:19:20,360
He just made that easier.

411
00:19:33,010 --> 00:19:34,700
What are you guys still doing here?

412
00:19:34,700 --> 00:19:36,700
I got this, go. Go home.

413
00:19:38,110 --> 00:19:39,620
You sure?

414
00:19:41,010 --> 00:19:42,400
Yeah, she's fed, she took her pills,

415
00:19:42,400 --> 00:19:44,540
she's all tucked in and watching TV.

416
00:19:44,540 --> 00:19:46,200
So, she's not too much for you?

417
00:19:46,200 --> 00:19:48,870
Are you kidding? I love her, she's great.

418
00:19:50,350 --> 00:19:53,760
Stewie, you gonna watch Wheel of Fortune with me?

419
00:19:53,760 --> 00:19:55,910
Coming, Debbie.

420
00:19:57,240 --> 00:19:58,880
You call her Debbie?

421
00:19:58,880 --> 00:20:00,240
She insisted.

422
00:20:00,240 --> 00:20:02,680
So, hey, guys, thank you so much.

423
00:20:02,680 --> 00:20:05,490
This job is a dream come true.

424
00:20:11,410 --> 00:20:13,590
Was that a little weird?

425
00:20:13,590 --> 00:20:15,310
Yeah. I don't know why,

426
00:20:15,310 --> 00:20:17,900
but something about it feels...

427
00:20:18,330 --> 00:20:20,470
unnatural.

428
00:20:22,380 --> 00:20:24,320
- Okay, let's go. - Yep.

429
00:20:26,840 --> 00:20:29,150
Okay, Sheldon, thanks for checking in.

430
00:20:29,150 --> 00:20:30,780
Talk to you tomorrow?

431
00:20:30,780 --> 00:20:33,050
O-Okay, bye.

432
00:20:33,580 --> 00:20:34,860
He's okay?

433
00:20:35,310 --> 00:20:37,300
Actually sounds like he's doing pretty well.

434
00:20:37,300 --> 00:20:39,840
I really think this is gonna be for the best.

435
00:20:39,840 --> 00:20:41,080
Me, too.

436
00:20:41,450 --> 00:20:43,150
And he was able to take a sabbatical from...

437
00:20:43,150 --> 00:20:45,890
How could you let him go?

